[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317488475","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118937#issuecomment-4317488475","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118937","id":4317488475,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAVelWw","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T02:00:05Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T02:00:05Z","body":"This is probably a stack overflow, given that the stack is a thousand frames deep. Interestingly, the parsing itself is not what's causing it, the overflow happens during codegen. Maybe it's worth converting `GDScriptCompiler::_parse_expression` to use a heap-based stack?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317488475/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317496218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118937#issuecomment-4317496218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118937","id":4317496218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAVfDmg","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T02:02:37Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T02:02:37Z","body":"Similar errors occur with\n```gdscript\ni = +++...+++i\n```\nand other recursive expressions","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317496218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317866993","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118937#issuecomment-4317866993","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118937","id":4317866993,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAV1r8Q","user":{"login":"AlgorithMagic","id":171487418,"node_id":"U_kgDOCjiwug","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171487418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic","html_url":"https://github.com/AlgorithMagic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlgorithMagic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T03:40:18Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T03:43:32Z","body":"From the chat in Discord, a depth guard came up which obviously is a simple quick fix, but I'm wondering if it would be practical to adapt the current AST to flatten left-associative binary/unary expression chains and lower them iteratively.  \n\nI haven't looked deeply yet into the issue but a shunting yard approach could be something to consider as well.\n\nAll this depending obviously on whether a limit fix is appropriate or not.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4317866993/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319116146","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118937#issuecomment-4319116146","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118937","id":4319116146,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAXB7cg","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T10:41:40Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T10:41:40Z","body":"How significant is this in practice? Replacing recursive descent with an alternative approach is a major change to the parser, which can lead to regressions. This seems unjustified if real projects don't encounter expression depths of this magnitude.\n\nNote that even replacing recursion with a loop doesn't formally guarantee the parser's applicability to unlimitedly deep expressions. There is a limit beyond which the loop counter will overflow. However, you'll likely encounter out-of-memory much sooner. I'm just pointing out that the parser's applicability to expressions of unlimited depth isn't a mandatory requirement, but is driven by practical considerations.\n\nThe only thing we can do with minimal effort is to add a reasonable limit on the recursion depth and throw an error when it is reached, stopping further parsing. This will prevent crashes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319116146/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320557450","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118937#issuecomment-4320557450","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118937","id":4320557450,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYZ5ig","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T21:08:08Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T21:08:08Z","body":"This specific error didn't happen in the parser, it happened at codegen. I think crashes in the parser are less likely overall, perhaps because they allocate less stack for each frame. I can try adding depth checks","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320557450/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]